    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Locating regions",
     "texto": [
      "**Nord**, **sør**, **øst** and **vest** are the compass points. **Nord for byen** means «north of the town»; expressions with **for** show relative position.",
      "**Kyst** is the coast and **innland** the interior of the country. **Region** is used for a wide area; it does not necessarily mean an official administrative area, such as an English county."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
